README.OSK -- how MNews and nn build on this diskThis directory is Ulrich Dessauer's MNews package as its archive carriedit (the Microware OS-9 archive's APPS/mnews.t.Z), with six files changedand each original kept beside it as `<file>.ori', as the package's owncopyright asks: changed sources travel with the originals.  NN_OSK/term.c      one line added: an `#endif' closing the `#ifdef                     HAVE_TERMIO' at line 348, which the file as                     distributed never closes.  Microware's cpp stops on                     it ("missing #endif").  NN_OSK/global.c    nn_owner() added and called in file_exist(): the                     library's stat() fills neither st_uid nor st_gid, so                     the owner tests compared the user's group with                     whatever the stack held, and for any user outside                     group 0 nn refused to save again to a file it had                     just made ("Cannot access").  The owner is read from                     the file descriptor instead (2026-09-25).  config.h           the article spool, /h0/SPOOL/NEWS -> /h0/SPOOL/MNEWS.  NN_OSK/config.h    the same for nn, and where nn finds the programs:                     /h0/ETC/CMDS -> /h0/CMDS/MNEWS.  On this disk                     SPOOL/NEWS is UUCPbb's news directory -- RBF names                     do not tell case apart -- so MNews gets its own.  NN_OSK/nnmisc.c,   the same /h0/ETC/CMDS -> /h0/CMDS/MNEWS in the path  NN_OSK/aux.c       each hands findmod().  RNEWS/mail.c       rnews mails through /h0/CMDS/UUCP/rmail, where this                     disk has one, instead of /h0/ETC/CMDS/rmail.These are the edits the package's own install notes ask for -- "editconfig.h and adapt it to your local system" -- carried into the threesource files that spell a path out instead of taking it from config.h.Everything else builds as it came.  What the build needs:  * TOP's os9lib: its library (GNULIB/os9lib.l) and its headers    (DEFS/os9lib), which the package was written against -- getgecos(),    the SysInfo calls, os9lib's own stat.h.  * Henry Spencer's regexp.h, which is NN_OSK/regexp.h; the functions    are in os9lib.l.  * strdup() and vsprintf(), from SRC/unixlib.  * error_log(), which the makefile expected from TOP's err.l.  No    archive here carries err.l, so the rebuild driver supplies a    one-function stand-in that writes the message to standard error.The makefiles install into /h0/ETC/CMDS, and inews, rnews, sbatch andnn look for one another there; the spool and library directories areset in config.h and NN_OSK/config.h.  At run time every program readsthe SysInfo data module -- TOP's system information table, which`setup' builds from a text file -- for the host name, the newsdirectories and its locks.